  "question": {
    "text": "The line of shortest distance between the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math> makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></msqrt></mfenced></math> with the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> in the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi></math> is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given lines,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now direction ratio&nbsp;of line of shortest distance will be,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now given angle between line and plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sin</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>27</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Now direction ratio of&nbsp;normal to plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mi>a</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mtext>as</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>given</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now equation of plane will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and image of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Note: This question was bonus in JEE mains 25th july 2022 paper, we have done some modification to the original question.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}